\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A material network represents effective constitutive behavior by composing parameterized building blocks. Expressivity concerns which response maps the architecture can represent; training fits its parameters using observed or simulated responses.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The constitutive class, building blocks, approximation loss, and training-data assumptions are unspecified.

Source-record limitation: The network building blocks, constitutive class, and proposed expressivity/training guarantees are unspecified.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Can Deep Material Networks be made more expressive through improved building blocks or hierarchies; why does elastic training suffice for inelastic applications; and can that theory improve training-data selection? \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2024/11}{[S2]}
